  "investigation_notes": "Diagnosis: `insufficient_evidence` \u2014 uploads failure confirmed as symptom, root cause not shown by available evidence.\n\nEvidence:\n- App is unhealthy: `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` on `/health` at two times (E2, E12).\n- Both containers `running`: `incidentlab-app-1 Up 5 seconds`, `incidentlab-db-1 Up 10 seconds (healthy)` (E1). DB inspect `running:true`, `health:healthy`, `oom_killed:false` (E7). App inspect `running:true`, `oom_killed:false`, `restart_count:0` (E3).\n- App container mount is present and writable-flagged: `bind source /srv/lab-data -> /data rw:true` (E3), running as `1000:1000` (E3).\n- Upload path permissions rule out simple owner/mode denial: `/srv/lab-data/uploads is_dir:true owner 1000:1000 mode 0755 app_user_can_write:true` (E10). Parent `/srv/lab-data` same (E11).\n- Recent recreation/restart observed: `kill/stop/die/destroy/rename/start` for app and db at `15:56:32` and `15:57:09` with `exit_code 0`, plus `health_status: healthy` for db (E6). This explains short uptimes in E1 but not the cause.\n- Critical sources unavailable, preventing root-cause determination: app logs `unavailable` (E4), db logs `unavailable` (E5), disk usage for `/srv/lab-data` `unavailable` (E8) and `/` `unavailable` (E9).\n\nWhy not conclude other causes:\n- Cannot conclude permission cause \u2014 E10 shows writable.\n- Cannot conclude DB-dependency cause \u2014 E1/E7 show db healthy, but without app logs (E4) DB connectivity from app viewpoint is untested.\n- Cannot conclude disk-full cause \u2014 E8/E9 unavailable.\n- Cannot conclude healthy \u2014 E2/E12 show 503.\n\nBudget used 12/12. Repairs not attempted per workflow; needs log and filesystem-capacity evidence after person approves.\n",
